    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe `nvim_exec2()` return documentation describes `output` as `string|nil`, which suggests the key is always present. When output capture is disabled, the returned dictionary has no `output` key.\n\n## Solution\n\nDescribe `output` as a string that is present only when `opts.output` is true. Update the source API comment and its generated help text together.\n\nThe existing `nvim_exec2` functional test covers both the empty dictionary and the captured-output dictionary. The documentation generator and functional suite were not run locally.\n\nFixes #24057\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-03T16:30:50Z",
